test(ai-dispatch): integration suite (#836) — second rework round

Original task: end-to-end integration tests for the AI dispatch flow
covering dispatch → orchestrator → adapter → terminal status, including
sensitive-output approval/release.

Round 2 changes (addressing the second code-review pass):
1. NEW classifier-flagged sensitive test (no purpose=contract, no caller
   hint): runner emits text with a PII pattern, heuristic classifier
   flags pii.email, row lands in pending_review, appears in approvals
   inbox, and is released via simulateDecideTaskApproval(approved). This
   complements the existing purpose=contract path so both sensitive
   surfaces are covered.
2. NEW dispatch-entrypoint boundary suite
   (`src/__tests__/dispatch-execution-task.boundary.test.ts`) — exercises
   the real `dispatchExecutionTask` helper from
   `src/lib/execution/dispatch.ts` against a mocked Supabase RPC.
   Verifies (a) the RPC name + argument shape, (b) `task_id` and `id`
   row-key mapping, (c) DispatchError is thrown on RPC error, and
   (d) DispatchError is thrown on missing data. Together with the
   integration suite this pins down the full caller→RPC→row→orchestrator
   chain.
3. Harness now save/restore-pairs `setStrictAgentRegistration` instead
   of leaving it permanently `false`, so other suites that run after
   the harness do not inherit relaxed agent registration.

Round 1 (kept from prior commit):
- Tests start from `simulateDispatch({domain, taskType, payload})` which
  mirrors `system.dispatch_execution_task` and returns a typed handle.
- Happy paths for ALL FOUR AI task types (completion, embedding, rag,
  tool-use) — distinct adapters, runner endpoints, agent slugs.
- Sensitive release/reject via `simulateDecideTaskApproval` mirroring
  the post-execute hold branch of the SQL RPC.
- Harness extracted to `src/__tests__/harnesses/ai-dispatch-harness.ts`
  as a shared, reusable module with generic `createDispatchHarness({...})`
  and AI-specific `buildAiDispatchHarness({...})`.

Files:
